<title>SINGAPORE: Germany says 29 countries signed up for ITA.</title>
<headline>Germany says 29 countries signed up for ITA.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty-nine countries have so far signed up for an agreement to liberalise world trade in information technology goods, German Economics Minister Guenter Rexrodt said on Thursday.</p>
<p>He told reporters the 29 accounted for 80 percent or more of world trade in infotech products.</p>
<p>In addition to the 15 members of the European Union, the countries signed up are Australia, Canada, Taiwan, Hong Kong, Iceland, Indonesia, Japan, South Korea, Norway, Philippines, Singapore, Switzerland, Turkey and the United States.</p>
<p>Rexrodt said he was confident that other countries would sign up by the deadline of March 15 so that the threshold of 90 percent stipulated in the deal worked out by the EU and the United States would be reached.</p>
<p>-- WTO newsroom 65 337 6070</p>
</text>
